## Delineation

/ [AlienHandIRCChatRefinementSource] -(Delineation)> [source_record_layer], [annotation_layer], [refined_product_layer], [runtime_interface_layer], [uncertainty]

& [DelineatedSubject: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the bounded subject that survived SJS delineation
  + [purpose] is to transform durable IRC conversation history into user-controlled refined products without mutating source chat evidence
  + [source_record_layer] is immutable raw conversation history, message payload identity, channel-scoped replay, and payload provenance
  + [annotation_layer] is bookmarks, bookmark notes, sticky references, quotes, and debug visibility attached to raw or refined anchors
  + [refined_product_layer] is cuts, chapters, editorial projections, edit diffs, and table-of-contents entries
  + [runtime_interface_layer] is The Lounge UI, local refinement HTTP API, SQLite storage, and app-owned runtime lifecycle hooks
  + [outside] is unrelated multi-mouse capture, Godot surface input, BizHawk runtime, and non-chat AlienHand app behavior
  + [uncertainty] is resizable pane divider behavior, polished quote selection, sticky presentation policy, editorial edit review UX, production authorization, and browser-click acceptance

  = must: preserve raw chat as source evidence
  = must: keep annotation and refinement artifacts derivative
  = must: keep runtime interfaces narrow enough to validate with local proofs
  = must: preserve uncertainty instead of treating rough prototype behavior as final product quality

## Exploded Specification

& [ExplodedSpecification: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the processed implementation-facing specification derived from the preserved source
  + [requirement_group] is source integrity, refinement object identity, storage, API, UI workbench, replay, search, annotation semantics, editorial semantics, runtime lifecycle, and verification
  + [non_goal] is replacement of IRC as the live coordination bus
  + [non_goal] is mutation of raw conversation history by chapters or edits
  + [non_goal] is final production authorization design in the prototype slice
  + [quality_bar] is source-preserving, replayable, channel-scoped, user-controlled, locally verifiable, and visually reviewable

& [CanonicalRequirement: SourceIntegrity] is the rule that raw conversation remains the durable evidence substrate
  + [raw_conversation] is immutable source chat history and payload references
  + [channel_scope] is one UUID-named IRC channel and its derived refinement state
  + [source_of_truth] is JSONL history plus immutable payload objects for raw chat, with SQLite refinement data treated as durable derived state

  = must: preserve raw chat records when blocks are copied into cuts
  = must: preserve payload and message identity through every derivative object
  = must: allow cold replay or storage sync to recover refinement source blocks
  - never: treat a chapter, edit, or UI projection as the source of truth

& [CanonicalRequirement: RefinementIdentity] is the object identity contract for the refinement layer
  + [conversation_block] is the smallest practical source-facing UI unit that can be promoted into cuts
  + [conversation_cut] is a selected instance of a block in a user-ordered cutting set
  + [conversation_chapter] is a derivative editorial grouping of cuts and source spans
  + [conversation_bookmark] is a navigational anchor with an optional attached note
  + [conversation_sticky] is a persistent working reminder attached to a block, cut, chapter, or bookmark
  + [conversation_quote] is a provenance-preserving excerpt
  + [conversation_edit] is a derivative transformation with before/after review evidence
  + [table_of_contents_entry] is ordered refined navigation for chapters and edit surfaces

  = must: assign stable IDs to every object
  = must: preserve backlinks from cuts, chapters, bookmarks, stickies, quotes, and edits to source anchors
  = must: support removed or superseded derivative state without deleting source records
  = should: keep notes as bookmark-attached annotations instead of a separate note feature

& [CanonicalRequirement: StorageAndIndexing] is the local persistence requirement for refinement data
  + [database] is SQLite for blocks, cuts, chapters, bookmarks, stickies, quotes, edits, edit diffs, TOC entries, and search mappings
  + [schema_version] is 1 for the current prototype
  + [json_fields] are canonical JSON text for tuple, reference, metadata, provenance, source scope, and diff content fields
  + [search_index] maps normalized terms back to source block IDs and may later expose cut or chapter context

  = must: migrate deterministically
  = must: make raw blocks and derived objects channel-queryable
  = must: preserve edit diffs as inspectable evidence
  = must: keep search results navigable back to source blocks
  = should: make future revisions additive migrations when possible

& [CanonicalRequirement: RefinementHTTPAPI] is the local service contract used by the browser workbench
  + [base_path] is /alienhand/refinement
  + [auth] is prototype bearer-token authorization shared with the payload resolver
  + [read_endpoints] are blocks, search, cuts, chapters, bookmarks, quotes, stickies, edits, edit-diffs, and toc
  + [write_endpoints] are adopt live block, create cut, remove cut, create chapter, create bookmark, create quote, create sticky, clear sticky, apply edit, and create toc entry

  = must: reject unauthenticated access when a resolver token is configured
  = must: validate target anchors before creating bookmarks, quotes, stickies, chapters, or edits
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled adoption of a live IRC line into a durable block
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled creation and soft removal of cuts
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled chapter creation, editorial edit creation, and TOC entry creation
  = should: remain UI-agnostic enough that other AlienHand clients can share it

& [CanonicalRequirement: TheLoungeWorkbench] is the browser-facing workbench contract for the AlienHand The Lounge fork
  + [entrypoint] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/components/Chat.vue
  + [workbench_component] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/components/AlienHandRefinementWorkbench.vue
  + [style] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/css/alienhand-chat.css
  + [fork_commit] is 4cd1e39d
  + [directory_frame] contains Nicks and Chapters tabs
  + [chat_frame] mounts the live The Lounge message list
  + [cutting_frame] shows selected cuts, insertion markers, and x removal controls
  + [editing_frame] shows plain projected text from cuts without chat bubble chrome or contributor labels
  + [bridge_arrow] is the large insertion arrow between Chat and Cutting

  = must: appear only for channel names that resolve to a 32-character hexadecimal UUID
  = must: provide independent Chat, Cutting, and Editing frame toggles
  = must: hide the bridge arrow whenever Chat or Cutting is hidden
  = must: let the user stage a live chat line and insert it into cuts at the current cut position
  = must: let dragging the bridge arrow update the insertion position in Cutting
  = must: let clicking an editing line reveal the source cut and source chat message when visible
  = must: expose raw JSON/debug state for review
  = should: remain visually reviewable before deeper polish work proceeds

& [CanonicalRequirement: AnnotationSemantics] is the user-visible meaning of bookmarks, notes, stickies, and quotes
  + [bookmark] is a navigation anchor that may exist in raw, refined, or both scopes
  + [note] is attached to the bookmark anchor and echoed into derived views
  + [sticky] is a persistent working reminder until cleared
  + [quote] is an exact excerpt or frame reference with provenance

  = must: mirror bookmarks into refined views where their source remains included
  = must: highlight bookmarked source blocks
  = must: show note text through hover, popup, or equivalent detail affordance
  = must: preserve quote provenance and source identity
  = should: make sticky references easy to clear without deleting durable history

& [CanonicalRequirement: EditorialSemantics] is the rule that editing creates derivative evidence instead of rewriting source
  + [editing_projection] is text derived from cuts or chapters with UI chrome stripped
  + [edit_diff] is the durable before/after evidence object
  + [toc] is the ordered navigation layer for refined chapters or edits

  = must: preserve pre-edit input refs and post-edit output refs
  = must: record edit type, reason, author, and diff evidence
  = must: keep editable text source-navigable to its originating cut and chat block
  = should: preserve code frames and media references as editorially usable blocks rather than flattening them into ambiguous prose

& [CanonicalRequirement: RuntimeLifecycle] is the local app-owned runtime requirement
  + [runtime_group] is Ergo, payload resolver, The Lounge, and UUID channel startup for live review
  + [live_review_command] is chat-workbench-live
  + [runtime_proof_command] is chat-workbench-runtime-proof
  + [launcher] is Launchers/run-chat-workbench-live.bat

  = must: start and stop the app-owned runtime group for review
  = must: publish at least one seeded message into a UUID channel for live review
  = must: write connection details before waiting
  = must: allow shutdown through stop file or Ctrl+C
  = should: support manual browser review until browser automation is available

## Constraint Check Trace

& [ConstraintCheckTrace: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the source-grounded constraint check for this SJS pass
  + [source_preservation] passed because the source snapshot records path, commit, hash, and line count before canonical output
  + [lineage] passed because every canonical requirement maps to the preserved source specification or its referenced foundation/platform docs
  + [source_integrity] passed because raw conversation immutability remains a top-level invariant
  + [boundary] passed because chat refinement excludes Godot input, multi-mouse capture, BizHawk, and non-chat runtime work
  + [implementation_truth] passed with uncertainty because existing prototype features are recorded separately from future polished behavior
  + [signature_readiness] passed because this file records stage set, trace, registry nodes, and satisfaction signature

  = must: preserve this trace with the canonical specification
  = must: rerun SJS if source hash changes or implementation contradicts a canonical requirement

## Pruning Trace

& [PruningTrace: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the cutback pass for unhealthy or premature specification growth
  + [pruned_material] is treating visual polish as already accepted, treating rough browser UI as final, embedding production authorization decisions in prototype UI, and absorbing Godot/multi-mouse work into the chat refinement subject
  + [preserved_frontier] is resizable pane dividers, quote selection polish, sticky presentation polish, editorial edit review polish, browser-click automation, production authorization hardening, and multi-client refinement synchronization
  + [repair] is canonical separation between implemented prototype workbench behavior and future polished product requirements

  = must: keep [preserved_frontier] visible for planning
  = must: avoid expanding this chat refinement spec into unrelated AlienHand input-surface architecture

## Exhaustion Review

& [ExhaustionReview: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the SJS pass termination review
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked
  + [reason] is source requirements repeatedly converge on source-preserving refinement objects, SQLite/API service contracts, The Lounge workbench UI, and explicit user-controlled transformation
  + [remaining_uncertainty] is implementation-facing and visual-polish-facing rather than core semantic uncertainty
  + [next_valid_work] is solution work against [OpenFrontier: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement]

  = must: stop abstract expansion unless new source material, source changes, or implementation contradiction appears
  = must: route future additions through source preservation and SJS reprocessing when they change the governing spec

## Justification

& [Justification: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the evidence bridge from source specification to canonical authority
  + [claim] is the chat refinement spec is stable enough to guide future AlienHand implementation
  + [support] is preserved source snapshot, prior runtime proofs in work-justification.sop, pushed The Lounge fork commit 4cd1e39d, and app-owned runtime launcher commit a2b5629
  + [support_type] is source_preservation, implementation_evidence, test_evidence, and bounded_uncertainty
  + [confidence] is high for source integrity, storage/API shape, and first workbench layout; moderate for final UX polish because visual review remains open
  + [counterargument] is browser-level acceptance has not yet been automated and the user may request further layout corrections after live review
  + [invalidation_condition] is source_change, failed_quality_gate, missing_trace, broken_lineage, registry_conflict, or implementation_contradiction

  ! [CanonicalSpecificationIsSufficientForNextImplementation] is accepted
    @ [support] [ConstraintCheckTrace: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement]
    @ [support] [PruningTrace: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement]
    @ [support] [ExhaustionReview: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement]

## Solution State

& [Solution: AlienHandIRCChatRefinementCurrentState] is the recorded implementation state at signing time
  + [implemented] is SQLite refinement storage, replay import, app-owned refinement storage lifecycle, authenticated local refinement HTTP API, bookmark/quote/sticky/editorial routes, The Lounge render adapter, live payload resolver fetch, workbench runtime proof, live review launcher, and full refinement frame layout in The Lounge fork commit 4cd1e39d
  + [partial] is visual workbench review, editing surface polish, quote selection controls, sticky presentation controls, and resizable pane divider behavior
  + [failed] is none known in this SJS pass
  + [leftovers] is [OpenFrontier: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement]
  + [verification] is unit/runtime proof history plus targeted The Lounge lint, stylelint, prettier, build, and live bundle string checks recorded in work-justification.sop
  + [deviation] is current Editing frame is a projected text surface, not yet a full rich editor with diff review UI

  = must: treat [implemented] as current solution evidence, not as a final UX acceptance claim
  = must: keep [partial] and [leftovers] visible before claiming completion

& [OpenFrontier: AlienHandIRCChatRefinement] is the implementation frontier after SJS signing
  + [frontier_item] is browser visual acceptance of the full Chat/Cutting/Editing layout
  + [frontier_item] is resizable pane divider sizing
  + [frontier_item] is polished quote selection and citation rendering
  + [frontier_item] is polished sticky pin presentation
  + [frontier_item] is editorial edit review and diff presentation
  + [frontier_item] is production authentication and authorization hardening
  + [frontier_item] is multi-channel and multi-client synchronization policy

  = must: select future work from this frontier unless new source material changes the spec
  = must: record future completed work as Solution plus Justification, not only as prose notes

